    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d613">

                <pb facs="0835" n="733" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg733"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/759: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Ethiopia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-08-08T17:00:00-04:00">August 8, 1935—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>43. The President has received the following message dated August 5 by telegraph
                    from the Emperor: “We desire to express our thanks for your statement to the
                    press on August 1st. Ethiopia has not ceased since beginning to seek peaceful
                    settlement and especially <pb facs="0836" n="734" xml:id="pg734"/> appreciates
                    the support of the Government and people of the United States in the cause of
                    peace.”</p>
                <p>The President desires you to acknowledge orally the receipt of the Emperor’s
                    message and to convey to him an appropriate expression of the President’s
                    appreciation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
